Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:33:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/67] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: Add Exynos9610

Add a compatible for the PMU of the Exynos9610. For now it is only used
as a syscon by the USB PHY, so it is listed with the plain syscon
variants; the vendor kernel describes it the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
index 5bd3987..4c810c2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ properties:
               - samsung,exynos5433-pmu
               - samsung,exynos7-pmu
               - samsung,exynos850-pmu
+              - samsung,exynos9610-pmu
               - samsung-s5pv210-pmu
           - const: syscon
       - items:
